# neutral.allow — the ruled exceptions to GATE-NEUTRAL (tools/neutral-check.py; LEDGER.md SR166; BP-shape-4, R16).
# One row per <repo-relative file> <token> found in a shared kernel file (unaos/crates/kernel/src minus arch/):
#   <file>  <token>  <reason>
# The reason is required (a row without one is a CONTROL failure, exit 2). A row that no longer matches the tree is
# STALE and fails the gate: the list only SHRINKS. A NEW board name in a shared file gets a subsystem name, not a row,
# unless it is data (a board IS the value) or a wire string the specs and evidence quote.
# Seeded by GATENEUTRAL at fb8ad2f4: every finding on that tip, none renamed (no kernel compile in the arc); each
# reason names the rename owed. Re-derive the list with `tools/neutral-check.py --emit`.

